From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 09:40:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: Mark the eMMC bus of the Cubie
 A7S as MMC only

The eMMC node of the Cubie A7S says non-removable and nothing else about
the card, so the MMC core treats it as a socket that may hold anything.
Every rescan of mmc_rescan_try_freq() then opens with an SDIO reset and
an SD attach (sdio_reset(), mmc_send_if_cond_pcie(), mmc_attach_sdio(),
mmc_attach_sd(); drivers/mmc/core/core.c), each guarded by
MMC_CAP2_NO_SDIO or MMC_CAP2_NO_SD, before mmc_attach_mmc() is reached.

SMHC2 only reaches the eMMC footprint U8 (schematic V1.10 page 9), which
is not fitted on every board, so no SD card and no SDIO function can ever
appear there. Add no-sd and no-sdio, which mmc_of_parse() turns into
those two bits, so the core goes straight to mmc_attach_mmc(), and on a
board without the eMMC it no longer sends SD and SDIO commands to an
empty bus either.

Not covered: mmc-ddr-1_8v, as sunxi-mmc already sets MMC_CAP_1_8V_DDR for
every host with new timings; the driver type (no fixed-emmc-driver-type,
nothing selects one) and the card's RST_n function, which stays as it is.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: on a board without the eMMC fitted, a re-probe
of SMHC2 sends no SD or SDIO command.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
index 475449dc57c3..b217ceea5135 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
@@ -377,6 +377,8 @@ &mmc2 {
 	vqmmc-supply = <&reg_cldo5>;
 	bus-width = <8>;
 	non-removable;
+	no-sd;
+	no-sdio;
 	cap-mmc-hw-reset;
 	mmc-hs200-1_8v;
 	mmc-hs400-1_8v;
